<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Harfush emirate</h1><p class="st-meta">1500 CE – 1865 CE (approx.) · capital Baalbek</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Shia dynasty of emirs who governed Baalbek and the northern Beqaa Valley under the Ottomans for more than three centuries.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Harfush were a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/twelver-shiism">Twelver Shia</a> clan who held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baalbek">Baalbek</a> and its district by the early Ottoman period. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>, who conquered <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syrian-arab-republic">Syria</a> in 1516, confirmed them as local governors and tax farmers, a role the family kept for generations.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">emirs</a> collected taxes from the farmers of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beqaa-valley">Beqaa</a> and passed revenue to the governors of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a>, keeping their own armed retainers. Their politics turned on rivalry and alliance with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/druze">Druze</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/man-dynasty">Ma'nids</a> and later the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shihab-dynasty">Shihabis</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mount-lebanon-emirate">Mount Lebanon Emirate</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yunus-al-harfush">Yunus al-Harfush</a> allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fakhr-al-din-ii">Fakhr al-Din II</a> before falling out with him; he was executed in 1625. The family protected the Shia community of the Beqaa.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Internal feuds and conflict with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shihab-dynasty">Shihabis</a> weakened them in the 19th century. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tanzimat">Tanzimat</a> reforms the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> removed the last <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">emirs</a> and exiled the family in the 1860s.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/harfush-emirate.jpg" alt="Harfush emirate" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Jeff Dahl · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rectangular_green_flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1500 CE – 1865 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Baalbek</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Yunus al-Harfush</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Twelver Shia Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/lebanon">Lebanon</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Harfush dynasty, Emirs of Baalbek</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1682&amp;focus=harfush-emirate" aria-label="Harfush emirate on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5602 945 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Harfush emirate lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5922 1201L5815 1335M5922 1201L5709 970"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5815 1335h0M5709 970h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5922 1201h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5922 1201h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Baalbek. <a href="/atlas?year=1682&amp;focus=harfush-emirate">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

